%description:

What a UE in another cell costs an uplink, against the closed form.

The uplink mirror of InterferenceDelta. computeUplinkInterference walks the
UEs other cells scheduled on the same bands and adds each one's received
power at the victim's base station. It is a different walk from the
downlink one -- over the Binder's uplink transmission map rather than over
the other cells' band status -- and it is the only place where a base
station's channel model evaluates a link to a UE it does not serve.

The scenario is two cells, a victim UE in the first and an interfering UE
in the second, run with uplinkInterference off and on. Every random
ingredient is switched off, so the wanted signal and the interferer's
contribution at the victim's base station are both the closed-form budget
LinkBudget grades, with the UE's transmit power and the base station's
noise figure:

    S = ueTxPower - PL(d_victim)      + Gtx + Grx - cableLoss
    I = ueTxPower - PL(d_interferer)  + Gtx + Grx - cableLoss
    N = thermalNoise + bsNoiseFigure

    SINR = S - 10 log10( 10^(N/10) + 10^(I/10) )

where d_interferer is the distance from the interfering UE to the victim's
base station. The walk has two branches, and each has its own statistic:
measuredSinrUl, the SINR the victim's base station computes for its CQI,
reads the current TTI's transmission map; rcvdSinrUl, the SINR of a data
reception, reads the previous TTI's. Either counts a band only if the other
cell scheduled the interferer on it. As in InterferenceDelta the reported
SINR therefore spans two endpoints, and both are asserted for both
statistics:

 - the maximum is the interference-free budget, from the TTIs in which the
   interferer was not scheduled;
 - the minimum is the fully-loaded budget, from the TTIs in which it was
   scheduled on every band.

With interference off the two extremes collapse onto one value.

%extraargs: -c InterferenceDeltaUl

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config InterferenceDeltaUl]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.MultiCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 3s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false
# The extremes are the quantities under test here, not the average.
**.measuredSinrUl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max
**.rcvdSinrUl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max

############### The sweep: the one thing that varies ##############
**.uplinkInterference = ${uli = false, true}
**.downlinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

############### Geometry: victim 100 m from its cell; the interferer 100 m from its own, 400 m from the victim's ##############
*.gnb1.mobility.initialX = 250m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialY = 500m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialZ = 10m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialX = 750m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialY = 500m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialZ = 10m
*.numUe = 2
*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[*].nrServingNodeId = 1
# Association is by best signal and then frozen: the victim must not change
# cell halfway through, or the budget it is graded against changes with it.
**.dynamicCellAssociation = true
**.enableHandover = false
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 350m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 500m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialX = 650m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialY = 500m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 1500m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: one path loss and nothing else ##############
**.scenario = "URBAN_MICROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 10m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false

############### The budget terms, stated rather than inherited ##############
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
**.numBands = 6
**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm
**.ueTxPower = 26dBm
**.antennGainEnB = 18dBi
**.antennaGainUe = 0dBi
**.cableLoss = 2dB
**.thermalNoise = -104.5dBm
**.ueNoiseFigure = 7dBm
**.bsNoiseFigure = 5dBm

############### Traffic: a trickle from the victim, a flood from the other cell ##############
*.ue[*].numApps = 1
*.server.numApps = 2
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrSender"
*.ue[*].app[0].destAddress = "server"
*.ue[0].app[0].destPort = 4000
*.ue[0].app[0].localPort = 4088
*.ue[0].app[0].packetSize = 40B
*.ue[0].app[0].samplingTime = 0.02s
*.ue[0].app[0].startTime = 0.1s
# Enough to keep the interferer scheduled most of the time, but not so much
# that it never falls idle: the check needs both extremes to occur.
*.ue[1].app[0].destPort = 4001
*.ue[1].app[0].localPort = 4089
*.ue[1].app[0].packetSize = 1000B
*.ue[1].app[0].samplingTime = 0.002s
*.ue[1].app[0].startTime = 0.05s
*.server.app[*].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.server.app[0].localPort = 4000
*.server.app[1].localPort = 4001

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=12 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
